First of all, try to take less damage.  Let your pet help kill off
monsters.  Once you can kill off rothes you'll be set for food because
the corpses start to be more nutritious.

In earlier versions of the game, starvation was much more common but
in 3.4.3 there are plentiful random food objects in Sokoban so keep an
eye on how much you have in your inventory until you have a few food
rations.  Also, take a look at the spoilers, or else experiment, on
what is safe to eat.  The early mummys and grid bugs won't do anything
for you but there are lots of gnomes to eat in the mines (quite often)
followed by a delicatessen in Minetown.  Make it a priority to either
find enough food in Minetown, get to Sokoban or just find sufficient
food from random pickups.

By the way, a piece of advice from my own repeated experiences.  While
it is certainly appropriate to use prayer as a means of dealing with
hunger, be careful of being greedy.  Once you have 3 or 4 food rations
you are probably better served saving your prayer for real help.
Nethack is a game of balance and being greedy or stingy can lead to
problems.  Also, if you have fat finger syndrome in Sokoban, make sure
your luck has recovered before praying for food.

What do you mean by "see most of a level"?  If you mean look at each
room, pick up the loot, kill some monsters and then go down, that's
fine.  But don't go digging for the vaults or messing about in the
shops until you have a bit of food.

